      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d8609626816d877243f3e7dcaff6006c257b35f648b12869b2a5a12c2bf92d8d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The sections form a hierarchy of representation changes rather than one literal physical system: lattice geometry becomes a quadratic form and Epstein zeta; prime-exponent vectors become many-body occupations and partition functions; convolution changes gas composition and statistics; partition or factorization constraints determine ensemble fluctuations; and Möbius sums or divisibility indicators become paths whose aggregate behavior encodes arithmetic cancellation or prime-factor statistics.",
